cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use the Materials Testing & Characterization Virtual Lab in teaching or research, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Materials Testing & Characterization Virtual Lab: an open virtual laboratory for mechanical testing, hardness, wear, NDT and metallography"
abstract: >-
  Browser-based virtual laboratory with 22 experiments in materials testing and
  characterization: tensile, compression, shear, torsion, bending, impact, fatigue
  and creep tests; Brinell, Rockwell and Vickers hardness; pin-on-disc wear;
  ultrasonic, magnetic particle and dye penetrant testing; specimen preparation,
  microstructure, grain size, Jominy, heat treatment, XRD and SEM/EDS. Each experiment
  provides pre- and post-tests, theory with nomenclature and a narrated explainer,
  a safety briefing, do-it-yourself machine set-up with interlocks, physics-based
  simulation, validation against handbook data, randomised numericals, and a
  watermarked lab report with uncertainty analysis.
authors:
